# Kernel config fragment: drop the unused multimedia ancillary drivers.
#
# Mirrors the following menuconfig changes, under
# "Device Drivers -> Multimedia support":
#
#   1. Un-select "Autoselect ancillary drivers (tuners, sensors, i2c, spi,
#      frontends)"   -> CONFIG_MEDIA_SUBDRV_AUTOSELECT=n
#      With autoselect off, Kconfig stops force-enabling every ancillary
#      driver and each one becomes individually selectable (and defaults to
#      off), which is what the rest of this fragment then pins down.
#
#   2. "Media ancillary drivers -> Customize TV tuners": deselect all of them.
#      None of these tuner chips exist on the Duo S (no analog/digital TV
#      front-end hardware at all), so every one of them is pure build time
#      and eMMC space.
#
#   3. "Digital TV options": turn everything off. CONFIG_DVB_CORE itself is
#      still pulled in by CONFIG_MEDIA_DIGITAL_TV_SUPPORT, but none of its
#      optional features are needed.
#
# Note: this fragment complements disable-dvb.config, which handles the DVB
# frontend/tuner *modules* themselves. Here we switch off autoselect and the
# ancillary TV tuner drivers.
#
# The camera path used on this board (CSI sensors via the Cvitek VI driver,
# plus UVC over USB) is untouched: CONFIG_MEDIA_CAMERA_SUPPORT,
# CONFIG_VIDEO_DEV, CONFIG_VIDEO_V4L2* and CONFIG_USB_VIDEO_CLASS all stay
# enabled.

# --- 1. no automatic selection of ancillary drivers ---
# CONFIG_MEDIA_SUBDRV_AUTOSELECT is not set

# --- 2. TV tuners (Media ancillary drivers -> Customize TV tuners) ---
# CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_SIMPLE is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_TDA18250 is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_TDA8290 is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_TDA827X is not set
